==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|fleugan|lang=non}}. Cognate with Old English ''[[fleogan|flēoġan]]'' (Modern English ''[[fly]]''), Old Frisian [[fliaga|fliāga]], Old Saxon [[fliogan]] (Dutch [[vliegen]]), Old High German [[fliogan]] (German [[fliegen]]). Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European ''*pleuk-''. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian ''[[plaũkti]]''.

===Verb===
